<!-- 14. PROGRAM STRUCTURE & GUI -->
<h1>8. PROGRAM STRUCTURE & GUI</h1>
<h2>8.1 Codebase Architecture</h2>
<p>The project is modularized into several core Python scripts to maintain a clean structure:</p>
<ul>
    <li><code>app.py</code>: Acts as the primary Streamlit frontend and routing server. It handles model loading, UI state, file uploads, and renders the Plotly charts.</li>
    <li><code>gradcam.py</code>: Encapsulates the explainable AI logic. It dynamically searches for the correct convolutional layer, manages the TensorFlow GradientTape, and blends the OpenCV heatmap.</li>
    <li><code>pyspark_pipeline.py</code>: The standalone big data module that initializes a SparkSession and handles distributed dataset querying and class distribution analysis.</li>
</ul>

<h2>8.2 Graphical User Interface (GUI)</h2>
<p>The user interface was built using Streamlit, themed with a professional dark navy and cyan aesthetic suitable for medical software. The dashboard is divided into interactive sections:</p>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Sidebar:</strong> Contains the drag-and-drop file uploader and dynamic application status metrics.</li>
    <li><strong>Diagnosis Card:</strong> Immediately presents the predicted tumor class and its severity.</li>
    <li><strong>Confidence Analytics:</strong> Utilizes Plotly gauge charts and radar charts to display class probabilities.</li>
    <li><strong>Grad-CAM Panel:</strong> A three-column layout showing the Original Scan, the Pure Heatmap, and the Blended Overlay side-by-side.</li>
    <li><strong>Clinical Insights:</strong> Expandable tabs providing relevant medical literature on symptoms, treatments, and statistics corresponding to the predicted tumor type.</li>
</ul>
<br>
