<p class="caption">Figure 4: Grad-CAM Original, Heatmap, and Overlay</p>

<!-- 17. LIMITATIONS -->
<h1>11. LIMITATIONS</h1>
<p>While the system is highly capable, it possesses certain practical limitations:</p>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Dataset Scope:</strong> The model was trained on a limited dataset of 2D MRI slices. It does not possess the temporal or spatial awareness required for 3D volumetric MRI analysis.</li>
    <li><strong>Grad-CAM is Not Segmentation:</strong> As a critical medical disclaimer, Grad-CAM highlights the regional pixels influencing the model's prediction; it does not perform exact, pixel-perfect medical boundary segmentation of the tumor.</li>
    <li><strong>Not a Diagnostic Replacement:</strong> The system is intended purely as a triage and secondary-opinion tool for educational and research purposes, not as a replacement for certified medical diagnosis.</li>
    <li><strong>Cloud Dependency:</strong> The architecture relies on active internet connectivity and AWS uptime to function.</li>
</ul>

<!-- 18. FUTURE SCOPE -->
<h1>12. FUTURE SCOPE</h1>
<p>The project lays a strong foundation for future advancements in cloud-native healthcare AI:</p>
<ul>
    <li><strong>U-Net Segmentation:</strong> Integrating a U-Net architecture alongside EfficientNet to provide exact tumor boundary masking in addition to classification.</li>
    <li><strong>Docker & Kubernetes:</strong> Fully containerizing the application using Docker and orchestrating it with Kubernetes to ensure auto-scaling during high-traffic periods.</li>
    <li><strong>Automated CI/CD Pipelines:</strong> Implementing GitHub Actions to automatically trigger tests and redeploy the EC2 instance whenever new code is pushed.</li>
    <li><strong>AWS EMR Integration:</strong> Migrating the current PySpark pipeline to a managed Amazon EMR cluster to process massive, multi-terabyte hospital databases in real-time.</li>
</ul>

<!-- 19. CONCLUSION -->
<h1>13. CONCLUSION</h1>
<p>This project successfully culminated in the development and deployment of an AI-powered Brain Tumor MRI Classification and Localization System. By fine-tuning the EfficientNet-B3 architecture, the system achieved high diagnostic accuracy across four distinct brain states. Crucially, the integration of Grad-CAM resolved the inherent black-box nature of deep learning, providing visual transparency that is vital for medical applications.</p>
<p>Furthermore, the project successfully demonstrated advanced DevOps and Cloud Computing proficiencies. By migrating the system from local environments to an AWS EC2 cloud infrastructure, setting up a secure virtual environment, and utilizing background daemons, the application achieved global, 24/7 accessibility. The inclusion of Apache PySpark further validated the system's readiness for large-scale clinical data pipelines. Ultimately, this system stands as a cohesive, professional-grade intersection of Machine Learning, Cloud Infrastructure, and scalable DevOps practices.</p>

